---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    Meaningless Charts is a small experiment in data literacy. Two real,
    independently sourced datasets get plotted on the same normalized chart —
    which makes them <em>look</em> connected, even when there's no reason to
    think they are.
  </p>
  <p>
    The data is real. The relationship is not.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every dataset here comes from a real public API — the World Bank, NASA, the USGS, Wikimedia
    — fetched by a script and checked before it's allowed anywhere near a chart. See
    <a href="/sources">Sources</a> for the full list and <a href="/methodology">Methodology</a>
    for exactly how pairings, normalization, and the fake insights are put together.
  </p>
</Layout>
